# Binaries must never be converted or diffed as text.
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.res binary
*.ico binary
*.bmp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.nupkg binary
*.p7s binary

# Deliberately no "* text=auto" rule here.
#
# Line endings in this repository are already mixed: sources and project files
# are stored with CRLF, README with LF. Adding text=auto would renormalize every
# CRLF blob to LF on the next commit, producing a repo-wide whitespace diff that
# breaks git blame and conflicts with every open fork and pull request. A plain
# "* -text" is no better: with core.autocrlf=true the working tree holds CRLF
# copies of blobs stored as LF, so freezing conversion would commit those back
# as CRLF and cause the same repo-wide diff in the other direction.
#
# Normalizing properly is a one-time, deliberate decision for the maintainer:
#   git add --renormalize .   (after adding "* text=auto" above)
# It should be its own commit, ideally when no pull requests are open.
